      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qigx1kc"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Ammonotelic animals (bony fish) excrete toxic ammonia, Ureotelic (mammals) excrete urea, and Uricotelic (birds, reptiles) excrete insoluble uric acid.",
        "Ultrafiltration takes place in the Malpighian corpuscle under high hydrostatic pressure in glomerular capillaries.",
        "Deficiency of Antidiuretic Hormone (ADH) leads to Diabetes Insipidus, resulting in excessive loss of water through dilute urine.",
        "Hemodialysis uses a cellophane membrane immersed in a dialyzing fluid to clear nitrogenous wastes from blood in patients with renal failure."
      ],
      "id": "6ic0gih"
